/* The camera permission sheet. Shown by iOS under "Own Hub would like to
   access the camera", the first time she opens it: for her national ID card,
   or for a meal she chooses to photograph. It names what is taken and what
   happens to it, because "to verify your identity" answers neither.

   Must stay in step with NSCameraUsageDescription in Info.plist and with
   ar.lproj/InfoPlist.strings. There is no photo-library key here, in either
   locale, because this app never asks for the library. */
"NSMotionUsageDescription" = "Own Hub uses your phone's motion only to tilt a few illustrations gently. Nothing is recorded or sent.";
"NSCameraUsageDescription" = "Own Hub uses the camera to photograph both sides of your ID card and take one selfie, so we can check that you are a woman, to photograph a meal if you choose so we can estimate what is on your plate, and to take a profile photo or coach photos if you choose. Nothing is uploaded until you tap send, analyse or submit. The ID card, selfie and meal photographs are read in memory and never stored. A profile photo you take stays on this phone. Photos you add as a coach (your photo, certificates, feedback and results) are uploaded for Own Hub to check, and the approved ones may be shown on your coach page. Photos and videos you choose to send in a coaching chat are uploaded to your coach.";
"NSMicrophoneUsageDescription" = "Own Hub uses the microphone only when you hold the mic button in a coaching chat to record a voice note, when you record a video with sound to send your coach, or when you tap the microphone to say what you ate. Nothing is recorded until you press, and a voice note is sent only when you let go. Voice notes and videos you send stay in the chat until you or your coach delete your account, so you can listen and watch again. When you say a meal, your phone turns your words into text that you check before anything is logged, and Own Hub does not keep the audio.";
"NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription" = "Own Hub uses speech recognition only when you tap the microphone to say what you ate. Your words become text that you check and fix before anything is logged. Where your phone can, this happens on the phone; otherwise Apple may process what you say to turn it into text. Own Hub does not keep the audio.";
